# Line endings, and which files are not text.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is configured for this clone, which means Git rewrites line
# endings on checkout and stores LF in the repository. That is the behaviour
# we want for source, and it is only safe if Git is never wrong about what is
# text. It would be wrong about the SQLite file if `data/` were ever
# un-ignored, and about any PNG that gets added later, so both are named here
# as binary.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.db    binary
*.db-journal binary
*.sqlite binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lock files are generated. A diff of them is never reviewable, and marking
# them as such keeps them out of the way without excluding them from the repo.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
